Yes. I went back through the work we covered over roughly the last 3 hours and compared it against the level expected for a Senior Quality Engineer / customer-facing QA automation role, including your experience and the framework you are preparing to demonstrate.

My honest assessment:

What we have built is good enough to demonstrate framework-design capability, but I would NOT go into the customer round with only what we have done so far.

The framework foundation is strong. We need a few important enterprise pieces and, more importantly, you need to be ready to explain the architectural decisions, not just show code.

Your resume positions you as a 13+ year senior QA/automation professional with Selenium, TestNG, REST Assured, CI/CD, parallel execution, framework architecture, JIRA integration and team leadership experience. So the customer is likely to evaluate you beyond "can you write Selenium code?"

