Final verdict

Yes, what we've done is good and technically credible.

But no, I would not yet say "nothing is missing." The biggest missing pieces are TestNG listeners/retry/data-driven execution, API + DB validation, CI/CD execution, and the senior-level strategy/leadership discussion.

And those matter because your profile is not being positioned as a junior Selenium developer. Your own experience shows Technical Lead responsibility, 13+ years, large automation programs, team leadership, framework architecture and release governance.

So our goal now should be:

Build enough of the framework to prove the architecture → then spend the majority of the remaining preparation making you capable of defending every architectural and QA decision in front of the customer.

That is what will materially improve your selection probability.